 "title": "Protein Function Annotation Methods and Tools",
 "summary": "This cluster is about various methods and tools used for protein function annotation. AUGUSTUS and AUGUSTUS+ are gene prediction tools developed by Stanke Mario, with AUGUSTUS+ using EST and having predictions for human chromosome 22. AnnoPRO is a method that uses multiple tools, including CAFA4, DeepGOPlus, NetGO3, PFmulDL, and others, to improve protein function annotation performance. Protein function annotation has seen improved performance with AnnoPRO and PFmulDL, but declined with DeepGOPlus and NetGO3. The cluster also includes various organisms, such as Homo sapiens, Drosophila melanogaster, and mus musculus, which have orthologs with each other.",
